# Reproduces the 2026-11-05 capture (claude 2.1.317, Haiku, stream-json, a throwaway repo with Shipline installed),
# docs/plans/shipline-chat-reliability.md "Results of the 2026-11-05 checks". Read by test/fixtures/fake-claude.mjs
# (# lines are comments, @ lines are directives, see its header). Values (ids, paths, tokens) are the fake's own.
# - stderr: the workspace-trust warning, printed twice (the server must send one banner). Captured text up to
#   "has not been trusted." and from "set projects[...]" on; the sentence between was elided in the plan's record.
# - system/init: mcp_servers {name, status, source} ({{MCP_SERVERS}}: the claude.ai Atlassian connector at
#   needs-auth unless the test sets FAKE_CLAUDE_MCP_SERVERS), slash_commands (all of them, including the
#   terminal-only ones, a plugin command and a skill) and terminal_slash_commands.
# - a hook's systemMessage: its own system/informational event, content "<Event>:<Tool> says: <message>".
# The turn waits for $FAKE_CLAUDE_RELEASE before system/init, so a test can look at a chat that has no init yet.
@wait-user
@stderr Ignoring 2 permissions.allow entries from .claude/settings.json: this workspace has not been trusted. Open it in interactive claude and accept the trust dialog, or set projects["{{CWD}}"].hasTrustDialogAccepted: true in ~/.claude.json
@stderr Ignoring 2 permissions.allow entries from .claude/settings.json: this workspace has not been trusted. Open it in interactive claude and accept the trust dialog, or set projects["{{CWD}}"].hasTrustDialogAccepted: true in ~/.claude.json
@wait-release
